  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ocean for Development Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ocean for Development Programme Mozambique. This is a bilateral institutional cooperation program between governmental institutions in Norway and Mozambique, with the overall goal to contribute to an &#x201c;enabling environment for sustainable social and economic development, including the importance of increased production and consumption of aquatic foods, contributing to improved food security, nutrition, and livelihoods&#x201d;. The program is focused around four main areas for cooperation: 1) integrated ocean management; 2), environment &#x2013; marine and coastal, 3) fisheries and aquaculture research and development; and 4) fisheries statistics. The framework agreement between Institute of Marine Research and Norad focuses on component 3 and 4: The aim is to strengthen the institutional and human capacity in developing sustainability in the fishery sector and in the emerging efforts to develop marine aquaculture, as well as improved fisheries statistics systems and infrastructure, as well as improved capacity and expertise for collection, analysing and dissemination.</narrative>
  </description>
